Meet Thomas, a man in his late thirties with a quiet and unassuming demeanor. He worked as an orderly at St. Mary's Hospital, a bustling facility in the heart of the city. Every day, Thomas would arrive at the hospital before dawn, donning his crisp white uniform and a smile that never wavered.

Thomas took great pride in his role as an orderly. His days were filled with tasks that many might consider mundane, but to him, each one was a vital part of ensuring the smooth operation of the hospital. He started by tidying up patient rooms, changing linens, and restocking supplies. His meticulousness was unparalleled; every surface shone, and every corner was free of clutter.

Beyond his cleaning duties, Thomas was also responsible for transporting patients to various departments within the hospital. He wheeled them gently, always mindful of their comfort and dignity. His gentle touch and soothing words often provided solace to those who were frightened or in pain. Patients and staff alike appreciated his calming presence, and it wasn't uncommon for them to seek him out for a kind word or a listening ear.

Thomas had an uncanny ability to anticipate the needs of others before they even realized it themselves. He knew which patients preferred extra blankets, which<|im_end|>

